 Pya N, Kneib T, et al. mgcv: Mixed GAM Computation Vehicle with GCV\/AIC\/REML smoothness estimation and GAMMs by REML\/PQL; 2016."},{"key":"bibr41-0272989X17738515","unstructured":"Plummer M. rjags: Bayesian Graphical Models using MCMC. R package version4-4. URL http:\/\/CRAN.R-project.org\/package=rjags; 2015."}],"container-title":["Medical Decision Making"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/journals.sagepub.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1177\/0272989X17738515","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/journals.sagepub.com\/doi\/full-xml\/10.1177\/0272989X17738515","content-type":"application\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/journals.sagepub.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1177\/0272989X17738515","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,1]],"date-time":"2026-05-01T17:59:08Z","timestamp":1777658348000},"score":65.31836,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/journals.sagepub.com\/doi\/10.1177\/0272989X17738515"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2017,11,10]]},"references-count":41,"journal-issue":{"issue":"2","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2018,2]]}},"alternative-id":["10.1177\/0272989X17738515"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1177\/0272989x17738515","ISSN":["0272-989X","1552-681X"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0272-989X","type":"print"},{"value":"1552-681X","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2017,11,10]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,21]],"date-time":"2026-08-21T18:40:24Z","timestamp":1787337624147,"version":"build-2736575974"},"reference-count":27,"publisher":"Society for Industrial & Applied Mathematics (SIAM)","issue":"3","funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000265","name":"Medical Research Council","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["MR\/S036709\/1"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["MR\/S036709\/1"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000265","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["SIAM\/ASA J. Uncertainty Quantification"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2020,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>We study Monte Carlo estimation of the expected value of sample information (EVSI), which measures the expected benefit of gaining additional information for decision making under uncertainty. EVSI is defined as a nested expectation in which an outer expectation is taken with respect to one random variable $Y$ and an inner conditional expectation with respect to the other random variable $\\theta$. Although the nested (Markov chain) Monte Carlo estimator has been often used in this context, a root-mean-square accuracy of $\\varepsilon$ is achieved notoriously at a cost of $O(\\varepsilon^{-2-1\/\\alpha})$, where $\\alpha$ denotes the order of convergence of the bias and is typically between $1\/2$ and $1$. In this article we propose a novel efficient Monte Carlo estimator of EVSI by applying a multilevel Monte Carlo (MLMC) method. Instead of fixing the number of inner samples for $\\theta$ as done in the nested Monte Carlo estimator, we consider a geometric progression on the number of inner samples, which yields a hierarchy of estimators on the inner conditional expectation with increasing approximation levels. Based on an elementary telescoping sum, our MLMC estimator is given by a sum of the Monte Carlo estimates of the differences between successive approximation levels on the inner conditional expectation. We show, under a set of assumptions on decision and information models, that successive approximation levels are tightly coupled, which directly proves that our MLMC estimator improves the necessary computational cost to optimal $O(\\varepsilon^{-2})$. Numerical experiments confirm the considerable computational savings as compared to the nested Monte Carlo estimator.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1137\/19m1284981","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,9,30]],"date-time":"2020-09-30T10:09:14Z","timestamp":1601460554000},"page":"1236-1259","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":9,"title":["Multilevel Monte Carlo Estimation of the Expected Value of Sample Information"],"prefix":"10.1137","volume":"8","author":[{"given":"Tomohiko","family":"Hironaka","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5445-3721","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Michael B.","family":"Giles","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6055-8055","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Takashi","family":"Goda","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Howard","family":"Thom","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"351","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,9,30]]},"reference":[{"key":"atypb1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1177\/0272989X04263162"},{"key":"atypb2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1177\/0272989X07302555"},{"key":"atypb3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1287\/mnsc.1110.1330"},{"key":"atypb4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s11009-013-9380-5"},{"key":"atypb5","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s00791-011-0160-x"},{"key":"atypb6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1142\/S021820251750021X"},{"key":"atypb7","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1137\/16M1096116"},{"key":"atypb8","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1287\/opre.1070.0496"},{"key":"atypb9","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S096249291500001X"},{"key":"atypb10","first-page":"425","author":"Giles M. B.","year":"2018","journal-title":"Springer"},{"key":"atypb11","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s11222-018-9835-1"},{"key":"atypb12","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1137\/18M1173186"},{"key":"atypb13","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1080\/07362994.2019.1705168"},{"key":"atypb14","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/sim.6983"},{"key":"atypb15","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1177\/0272989X17715627"},{"key":"atypb16","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1214\/10-AOP541"},{"key":"atypb17","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.3150\/12-BEJ442"},{"key":"atypb18","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"J. S. Liu,\n                      Monte Carlo Strategies in Scientific Computing\n                      , Springer, 2004.","DOI":"10.1007\/978-0-387-76371-2"},{"key":"atypb19","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1177\/0272989X15583495"},{"key":"atypb20","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"C. P. Robert and G. Casella,\n                      Monte Carlo Statistical Methods\n                      , 2nd ed., Springer, 2004.","DOI":"10.1007\/978-1-4757-4145-2"},{"key":"atypb21","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1137\/16M1061692"},{"key":"atypb22","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/0266-5611\/29\/6\/065011"},{"key":"atypb23","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1051\/m2an\/2016005"},{"key":"atypb24","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s00211-020-01131-1"},{"key":"atypb25","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1177\/0272989X15575286"},{"key":"atypb26","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S0962492910000061"},{"key":"atypb27","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"N. J. Welton, A. J. Sutton, N. J. Copper, K. R. Abrams, and A. E. Ades,\n                      Evidence Synthesis for Decision Making in Healthcare\n                      , Wiley, 2012.","DOI":"10.1002\/9781119942986"}],"container-title":["SIAM\/ASA Journal on Uncertainty Quantification"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/epubs.siam.org\/doi\/pdf\/10.1137\/19M1284981","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"da